ess as we know it.\n   \n\n  \n\n* Agentic Frameworks:\n+ Design, Develop , fine\\-tune, and deploy Generative AI models with a focus on RAG frameworks to enhance information retrieval and generation.\n+ Develop and optimize LLM\\-based agents for tasks like knowledge grounding, multi\\-step reasoning, and decision\\-making.\n+ Integrate external data sources (e.g., vector databases) with LLMs to build dynamic, context\\-aware systems.\n\n\n* Architecture; Scalability:\n+ Develop scalable, distributed AI systems with a focus on performance, fault tolerance, and disaster recovery.\n+ Develop detailed design specifications, including modular, extensible, and functional component\n+ Develop MVP's into Shippable product to validate requirements and refine designs iteratively.\n+ Provide deeper Insights on Containerization/Docker (and) experience in CI/CD and deployment pipelines\n\n\n* Collaboration; Product Integration:\n+ Work cross\\-functionally to design solutions that address both functional and non\\-functional requirements.\n+ Establish best practices for building and maintaining AI\\-driven systems.\n+ Drive technical direction for large\\-scale AI initiatives and mentor junior engineers.\n+ Hands on engineer who can build tech stack ground up and deploy scalable solution\n\n\n* Product Development :\n+ Creating highly resilient distributed systems capable of operating reliably across large fleets of retail devices with remote observability and recovery\n\n\n What you'll bring:\n   \n\n  \n\n* Overall 12\\+ years of experience in machine learning / software engineering, with 2\\+ years in Generative AI or LLMs\n* Strong experience with Agentic Frameworks, RAG frameworks, vector search technologies and knowledge grounding techniques.\n* Expertise in Python, ML frameworks (PyTorch, TensorFlow), and libraries like Hugging Face Transformers.\n* Clear Communication, including the ability to build design gaps\n* Ability to multitask between several different requirem