ly in German as well\n* Based in Munich or willing to relocate for the duration of the internship\n\n\n We appreciate your application even if you don't tick all the boxes.\n   \n\n  \n\n**What We Offer**\n* Real ownership from day one\n* A fast\\-track into a full\\-time role\n* Direct mentorship from senior engineers and direct access to founders\n* Hands\\-on experience onsite with real customers, real production systems, and frontier AI\n* A fast\\-paced environment backed by the world's best investors, with the world's leading organizations as customers\n\n\n Want to build real things at the edge of industrial AI? Apply now.\n   \n\n  \n\n Apply now\n   \n\n  \n\n See more open positions at Manex AI","https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4428528662":"**Role Description** \n This part\\-time remote Data Analyst / Data Scientist role at DALVIARQ \\- Aluminio y Cristal focuses on turning business and operational data into actionable insights. You will collect, clean, and validate data from multiple sources, build datasets, and design dashboards and reports to support decision\\-making. Day\\-to\\-day responsibilities include performing exploratory data analysis, applying statistical methods, and developing predictive or descriptive models to understand trends in production, sales, and project performance. You will collaborate with cross\\-functional stakeholders to define data requirements, translate business questions into analytical tasks, and clearly present findings and recommendations. The role also involves documenting methodologies, maintaining data quality standards, and suggesting process improvements based on data\\-driven evidence.\n   \n\n**Qualifications**\n* Strong analytical skills, including the ability to break down complex problems, identify patterns, and propose data\\-driven solutions.\n* Proficiency in data analytics, including data cleaning, transformation, visualization, and dashboard creation using common analytics tools.\n* Applied knowledge