 the stack, talking to users, and shipping impactful products at high velocity.\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n You'll help design, build, and scale systems spanning product experiences, backend infrastructure, workflow automation, and AI\\-powered capabilities while playing a key role in shaping what gets built next.\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n What You'll Do\n \n\n\n* Build and ship end\\-to\\-end product features across frontend and backend systems.\n* Design and develop high\\-performance user\\-facing applications using modern web technologies.\n* Architect scalable backend services, APIs, and data models.\n* Build and improve AI\\-powered workflows, automation systems, and agent\\-driven experiences.\n* Work directly with users to understand pain points and translate them into product solutions.\n* Develop real\\-time systems, integrations, and workflow orchestration capabilities.\n* Improve platform reliability, security, multi\\-tenancy, and operational scalability.\n* Contribute to product strategy, technical direction, and architecture decisions.\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n You're a Great Fit If You\n \n\n\n* Have 5\\+ years of experience building and shipping production software.\n* Possess strong TypeScript and backend engineering expertise.\n* Have experience building full\\-stack applications using modern frontend frameworks.\n* Have strong experience with PostgreSQL and modern application architectures.\n* Are comfortable working across product, engineering, and customer\\-facing discussions.\n* Thrive in fast\\-paced startup environments with high ownership and ambiguity.\n* Demonstrate strong engineering judgment and problem\\-solving skills.\n* Can independently take ideas from concept to production.\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n Bonus Points If You Have\n \n\n\n* Experience building AI agents, LLM\\-powered applications, or workflow automation systems.\n* Experience with real\\-time systems and WebSocket\\-based architectures.\n* Startup or founding engineer experience.\n* Exposure to healthcare, healthtech, or operational workflow platforms.\n* Experience with multi\\-tenant SaaS platforms and integrations.\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n Why Join Us?\n \n\n\n* Work on AI products solving meaningful real\\-world healthcare challenges.\n* Own critical product decisions and see your work reach production quickly.\n* Collaborate directly with users and shape the future product roadmap.\n* Join a high\\-caliber engineering team focused on speed, quality, and impact.\n* Receive meaningful equity alongside a highly competitive compensation package.\n* Build at the intersection of product engineering, AI, and healthcare innovation.","https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4428539292":"**Role Description** \n The Data Analyst / Data Scientist will support the Regional Integration Network for International Professionals in Berlin by turning complex data into actionable insights that improve services and outcomes for internationally recruited talent and partner organizations. This part\\-time, remote role includes collecting, cleaning, and validating data from various internal and external sources, as well as designing and maintaining dashboards and reports for stakeholders. The position involves conducting exploratory and statistical analyses, building and refining data models, and translating findings into clear recommendations for program design and policy decisions. The role also includes collaborating with cross\\-functional teams to define KPIs, documenting methodologies and data pipelines, and ensuring data quality, privacy, and compliance with relevant regulations.\n   \n\n**Qualifications**\n* Strong analytical skills and proven experience in data analytics to evaluate trends, patterns, and performance indicators.\n* Solid foundation in statistics, including hypothesis testing, regression, and basic experimental design, to support evidence\\-based decision\\-making.\n* Experience with data modeling and working with relational databases or data warehouses to structure and optimize data for analysis.\n* Clear and effective communication skills to present complex analytical results in an accessible way to non\\-technical stakeholders.\n* Proficiency with analytical and visualization tools (e.g., Python or R, SQL, Excel, and BI tools such as Power BI or Tableau).\n* Understanding of data privacy, security, and ethical handling of sensitive information, ideally within a public or social sector context.\n* Bachelor’s degree or equivalent experience in Data Science, Statistics, Computer Science, Economics, Social Sciences, or a related field.\n* Ability to work independently in a remote, part\\-time setting, manage multiple priorities, and collaborate effectively in diverse, multicultural teams.\n* Interest or experience in labor markets, migration, integration, or public administration is an advantage; working proficiency in English is required, and German skills are beneficial.","https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4428532396":"Thank you for your interest in the backend developer role.\n   \n\n  \n\n**Some Things To Note**\n* This role is specifically for individuals located in LATAM (Spanish America and Brazil).\n* This is a contracted position.\n* Please fill our the following details fully for consideration.","https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4428551292":"**Role Description** \n This is a part\\-time, remote role for a Full Stack Software Engineer on the Billing Team at Agentur für Internationale Museumskooperation. You will design, build, and maintain billing\\-related features across the full stack, ensuring accurate invoicing, payment processing, and reporting for our museum partners. Day\\-to\\-day responsibilities include implementing and refining front\\-end interfaces for billing workflows, developing and optimizing back\\-end services and APIs, and integrating with external payment and accounting systems. You will collaborate closely with product, finance, and other engineering team members to clarify requirements, estimate work, and deliver incremental improvements. The role also includes writing automated tests, reviewing code, monitoring system performance, and participating in continuous improvement of our development practices and technical architecture.\n   \n\n**Qualifications**\n* Strong Full\\-Stack Development and Software Development skills, with experience delivering production web applications end to end.\n* Proficiency in Front\\-End Development and Cascading Style Sheets (CSS) to build accessible, responsive, and user\\-friendly billing interfaces.\n* Hands\\-on experience in Back\\-End Web Development, including RESTful APIs, data modeling, and integration with third\\-party payment or accounting services.\n* Ability to work effectively in a remote, part\\-time setting, including clear communication, time management, and collaboration in distributed teams.\n* Familiarity with modern frameworks and tools (e.g., React or similar front\\-end libraries, Node.js/Java/.NET or comparable back\\-end stacks, relational databases).\n* Experience with version control (Git), code review practices, and automated testing (unit, integration, or end\\-to\\-end).\n* Comfort working with financial or transactional data, with attention to detail, data integrity, and security best practices.\n* Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or equivalent practical experience; experience in cultural, nonprofit, or public sector domains is a plus.","https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4428542383":"**Company Description** \n Serverwala Global is an industry\\-leading data center provider established in 2015, helping businesses build and scale their online presence. Headquartered in Jaipur with branches in Surat, Nasik, and Dubai, the company operates numerous data centers worldwide. A team of 50\\+ professionals focuses on continuously upgrading server technologies and delivering reliable, enterprise\\-grade resources. Serverwala offers a wide range of s