ion, and stakeholder management skills, with the ability to represent the company externally.\n* Entrepreneurial mindset, data\\-driven decision\\-making, and comfort working in a fast\\-moving, global environment.\n* Bachelor’s degree in Business, Computer Science, Engineering, or a related field preferred; equivalent experience considered.","https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4428546543":"Hiring: Data Scientist (United States)\n \n We are currently seeking a highly motivated and data\\-driven Data Scientist to join our growing analytics and AI team in the United States.\n \n\n\n Position:\n \n Data Scientist\n \n\n\n Location:\n \n United States\n \n\n\n Job Type:\n * Full\\-Time / Part\\-Time\n* Remote / Hybrid Available\n\n\n Responsibilities:\n * Analyze large\\-scale structured and unstructured datasets to uncover actionable insights\n* Develop machine learning models, predictive analytics solutions, and statistical frameworks\n* Design and conduct experiments, A/B tests, and performance evaluations\n* Collaborate with engineering and business teams to solve complex business challenges\n* Build data pipelines and automate analytical workflows\n* Create dashboards, reports, and visualizations to communicate findings effectively\n* Deploy and monitor machine learning models in production environments\n\n\n Requirements:\n * Bachelor's or Master's degree in Data Science, Statistics, Mathematics, Computer Science, or a related field\n* Strong proficiency in Python, R, SQL, and data analysis techniques\n* Experience with machine learning frameworks such as Scikit\\-learn, TensorFlow, or PyTorch\n* Knowledge of statistical modeling, predictive analytics, and data mining\n* Experience with cloud platforms such as AWS, Azure, or Google Cloud\n* Familiarity with data visualization tools such as Tableau, Power BI, or Looker\n* Strong analytical, problem\\-solving, and communication skills\n\n\n Benefits:\n * Competitive salary package\n* Flexible working environment\n* 